body:
This CSP guidance is incomplete: the `Function` constructor itself requires allowing `unsafe-eval` in CSP (in addition to any dynamic import allowances). Please adjust the comment so users don’t interpret this as only a dynamic-import restriction.
```suggestion
        // CSP Consideration: This pattern relies on the Function constructor plus
        // dynamic import(). In a strict Content Security Policy, this typically
        // requires allowing 'unsafe-eval' in script-src (for Function) and ensuring
        // that dynamic module imports from the widget origins are permitted. If you
        // cannot relax CSP to allow this, use 'inline' or 'registry' source types
        // instead of 'module'.
```
